---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Interim Terms of Use - CUNY AI Lab">
  <PageHero containerClass="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-200">Interim policy · Version 2026-09-19-interim</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold font-display text-white tracking-tight">CUNY AI Lab Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/90">These terms govern use of the Lab’s current services.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <main class="bg-white py-14">
    <article class="policy max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p><strong>Effective September 19, 2026.</strong> These terms apply to the CUNY AI Lab website, Sandbox, Dashboard, API keys, Media Tools, Agent Studio, Site Studio, and other services presented as part of the Lab.</p>

      <h2>Purpose and access</h2>
      <p>CAIL is an experimental environment for teaching, research, and academic work. Features, models, limits, and availability may change as the Lab develops its services.</p>
      <p>Access is tied to your verified CUNY identity. Do not share your account, session, class invitation link, or API keys with others, and use them only for the purposes they were issued for. Your access may have an end date and an assigned allowance. Your <a href="https://tools.ailab.gc.cuny.edu/model-access/">Dashboard</a> shows the allowance and reporting period assigned to you.</p>

      <h2>Responsible use</h2>
      <p>Users are responsible for using our services in accordance with applicable law, CUNY policy, their campus rules, and instructions from their instructor or program. The current <a href="https://www.cuny.edu/about/administration/offices/cis/it-policies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CUNY IT policy page</a> includes the Policy on Acceptable Use of Digital Assets and Resources and the Data Classification Standard.</p>
      <p>Do not use the services to gain unauthorized access, disrupt systems, impersonate another person, distribute malware or spam, harass people, or create or share unlawful material. Do not use CAIL for medical, legal, financial, safety, disciplinary, or other consequential decisions.</p>

      <h2>AI output and academic work</h2>
      <p>Models can produce inaccurate, incomplete, biased, or fabricated output. You are ultimately responsible for the material you submit, for verifying the output, and for meeting copyright, privacy, attribution, and other obligations in any work you produce with it. Course use must follow the instructor’s directions and the <a href="https://policy.cuny.edu/general-policy/article-i/#policy-1.03" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CUNY Academic Integrity Policy</a>.</p>
      <p>Similar or identical output may be produced for other users.</p>

      <h2>Data and privacy</h2>
      <p>Do not submit confidential data, FERPA-protected education records, HIPAA-regulated information, government identifiers, private personnel information, or other sensitive personal data unless CUNY has specifically approved the service and use. Please refer to our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Notice</a> for information about what the Lab stores and what is sent to model providers.</p>

      <h2>Classes and instructor responsibilities</h2>
      <p>An instructor or class organizer who applies for class access is responsible for giving students the approved class invitation link and making sure they use that link rather than submit individual applications. Because CAIL operates with limited staff, the Lab itself can only help with technical issues and, for approved pilot courses, pedagogical support. Instructors are therefore responsible for providing first-line support with access and usage, and for giving students basic guidance on Sandbox use, course rules, and responsible AI practice, including basic hygiene and best practices for AI use such as keeping unrelated work in separate chats, checking model output, and not entering sensitive personal information.</p>
      <p>Each student is required to accept these terms individually upon joining a class. Acceptance by an instructor or class organizer does not extend to the students in that class.</p>

      <h2>Allowances, suspension, and service changes</h2>
      <p>CAIL may assign different allowances, reporting periods, tools, or access dates to different users and classes. Separate written or funded arrangements may apply. When you use up your allowance, model requests pause until your reporting period resets. Except in extraordinary circumstances, the Lab will not reset or raise an allowance before then.</p>
      <p>The Lab may restrict or suspend access to protect users and systems, enforce these terms, comply with CUNY requirements, or respond to resource limits. Experimental services may be changed or discontinued. Do not rely on CAIL as the only copy of important work.</p>

      <h2>Updates and questions</h2>
      <p>The version number at the top of this page tells you which terms you accepted. If we make a change that requires your acknowledgement, we will ask you to review and accept the new version before you continue using the services. Questions may be sent to <a href="mailto:ailab@gc.cuny.edu">ailab@gc.cuny.edu</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .policy { color: #374151; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .policy h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: .65rem; color: #1D3A83; font-family: Outfit, sans-serif; font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .policy p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .policy a { color: #2A6FB8; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
